<section id="cost" class="section"><div class="container"><div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 reveal"><span class="section-eyebrow">Budget</span><h2 class="heading-lg text-3xl md:text-4xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">How Much Does a Trip to China Cost?</h2><p class="body-text text-lg">Realistic budget estimates based on travel style, with a detailed breakdown.</p><p class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mt-3">Estimates from our independent research, August 2026 (USD). Prices vary by season, city, and booking platform. Excludes international flights.</p></div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8"><div><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Travel Style</th><th>Per Day (USD)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Budget</td><td>$50-100</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Mid-range</td><td>$100-200</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Luxury</td><td>$250+</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="body-text text-xs mt-3">* Includes accommodation, food, transport, and activities. Excludes international flights.</p><div class="mt-6 card p-5"><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">Example Trip Totals (mid-range, 14 days)</h3><ul class="space-y-1.5 body-text text-sm"><li><strong>Couple (2 adults):</strong> approx. $2,800–5,600 total — 2 people × 14 days × $100–200/day</li><li><strong>Family of 4 (2 adults + 2 kids):</strong> approx. $4,200–8,400 total — kids pay 30–50% less for attraction tickets and usually share rooms</li><li><strong>Solo traveler:</strong> approx. $1,400–2,800 total — single occupancy raises the per-person cost</li></ul><p class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mt-3">Children under 6 often enter attractions free; ages 6–18 typically pay half price. Excludes international flights.</p></div></div><div class="card p-6"><h3 class="heading-md text-xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">Quick Cost Calculator</h3><form id="cost-calc" class="space-y-4"><div><label class="block text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Travelers</label><input type="number" id="cost-travelers" min="1" max="10" value="2" class="w-full rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] px-4 py-2.5 text-sm bg-white focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[var(--color-accent)] focus:border-transparent"></div><div><label class="block text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Days</label><input type="number" id="cost-days" min="1" max="60" value="14" class="w-full rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] px-4 py-2.5 text-sm bg-white focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[var(--color-accent)] focus:border-transparent"></div><div><label class="block text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Travel Style</label><select id="cost-style" class="w-full rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] px-4 py-2.5 text-sm bg-white focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[var(--color-accent)] focus:border-transparent"><option value="budget">Budget ($75/day)</option><option value="mid" selected>Mid-range ($150/day)</option><option value="luxury">Luxury ($300/day)</option></select></div><button type="button" id="cost-submit" class="btn-primary w-full">Calculate</button></form><div id="cost-result" class="mt-6 hidden"><div class="border-t border-[var(--color-border-light)] pt-4"><p class="body-text text-sm">Estimated Total (per person)</p><p id="cost-output" class="heading-lg text-3xl text-[var(--color-accent)]"></p><div id="cost-breakdown" class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-xs"><div class="flex justify-between"><span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">Accommodation</span><span id="cost-hotel" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-text)]"></span></div><div class="flex justify-between"><span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">Food &amp; Drink</span><span id="cost-food" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-text)]"></span></div><div class="flex justify-between"><span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">Transport</span><span id="cost-transport" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-text)]"></span></div><div class="flex justify-between"><span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">Activities</span><span id="cost-activities" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-text)]"></span></div><div class="flex justify-between"><span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">Misc</span><span id="cost-misc" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-text)]"></span></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><section id="visa" class="section-alt"><div class="container"><div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 reveal"><span class="section-eyebrow">Entry</span><h2 class="heading-lg text-3xl md:text-4xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">Do You Need a Visa for China?</h2><p class="body-text text-lg">China visa rules are changing fast. Here is what you need to know.</p><p class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mt-3">Sources: China National Immigration Administration (en.nia.gov.cn) and Chinese embassies/consulates. Rules verified August 2026 — policies change frequently, always confirm with your local Chinese embassy before booking.</p></div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5 mb-10 stagger-children reveal"><div class="card p-5"><div class="tag mb-2">L Visa required</div><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">USA &amp; other non-exempt countries</div><div class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Apply at Chinese embassy/consulate before travel. Single-entry 30-day tourist visa ~$140. Processing: 4–10 business days.</div></div><div class="card p-5"><div class="tag mb-2">240-hour visa-free (10 days)</div><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">55 countries (transit)</div><div class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Stay up to 10 days when transiting to a third country/region. Must hold a confirmed onward ticket. Travel freely across 24 provinces via 60+ designated ports.</div></div><div class="card p-5"><div class="tag mb-2">30-day visa-free</div><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">Singapore, Japan, Korea, Malaysia, Thailand + more</div><div class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Ordinary passport holders from 40+ countries (Asia, Europe, Oceania, Americas) can enter China visa-free for up to 30 days for tourism or business.</div></div><div class="card p-5"><div class="tag mb-2">30-day visa-free (2026 trial)</div><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">UK, Canada (until Dec 31, 2026)</div><div class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">British and Canadian passport holders enjoy visa-free entry for up to 30 days — trial period running through December 31, 2026.</div></div></div><div class="card p-6 max-w-3xl reveal reveal-delay-2"><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">240-Hour Transit-Free Ports</h3><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"><span class="tag">Beijing</span><span class="tag">Shanghai</span><span class="tag">Guangzhou</span><span class="tag">Shenzhen</span><span class="tag">Chengdu</span><span class="tag">Xi&#39;an</span><span class="tag">Chongqing</span><span class="tag">Kunming</span><span class="tag">Xiamen</span><span class="tag">Qingdao</span><span class="tag">Wuhan</span><span class="tag">Hangzhou</span><span class="tag">Nanjing</span><span class="tag">Tianjin</span><span class="tag">Dalian</span><span class="tag">Shenyang</span><span class="tag">Guilin</span><span class="tag">Changsha</span><span class="tag">Harbin</span><span class="tag">Ningbo</span><span class="tag">Zhengzhou</span></div><p class="body-text text-xs mt-4">Policy covers 24 provinces with 60+ designated ports. Must hold a confirmed onward ticket to a third country/region. Travel within the 24 covered provinces is allowed.</p></div><div class="max-w-3xl mt-10 reveal reveal-delay-3"><h3 class="heading-md text-xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">How to Apply for a China Tourist Visa (L Visa)</h3><div class="card p-6"><ol class="space-y-4"><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">1</span><div><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Check if you need a visa</div><div class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] mt-0.5">Many nationalities need an L visa. Check your local Chinese embassy website for the latest rules — visa policies change frequently. Currently, 55 countries have 240-hour (10-day) transit-free access, and citizens of 40+ countries enjoy 30-day visa-free entry.</div></div></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">2</span><div><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Gather required documents</div><div class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] mt-0.5">Valid passport (6+ months validity, 2+ blank pages). Completed visa application form (COVA, filled online). Recent passport photo (48mm x 33mm, white background). Round-trip flight itinerary + hotel bookings. Detailed travel itinerary. Bank statements (last 3 months) showing sufficient funds.</div></div></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">3</span><div><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Submit your application</div><div class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] mt-0.5">Most countries: submit in person at the nearest Chinese embassy/consulate or visa application center (CVASC). Some countries allow postal applications. No appointment system in most locations — arrive early (before 9am) to avoid long queues. Biometric data (fingerprints) collected on site.</div></div></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">4</span><div><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Pay and wait</div><div class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] mt-0.5">Standard L visa fee: approximately $140 (varies by nationality and reciprocity). Processing time: 4-10 business days (standard), 2-3 business days (express, extra fee). Single-entry 30-day tourist visa is the most common for first-time visitors. 10-year multiple-entry visas available for US citizens ($140).</div></div></li></ol></div><div class="card p-6 mt-5"><h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">Common Rejection Reasons &amp; Pro Tips</h4><ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]"><li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-red-500 font-bold mt-0.5">&#10007;</span><span><span class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Incomplete itinerary:</span> You must provide hotel bookings for every night. Book refundable hotels if your plans are flexible.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-red-500 font-bold mt-0.5">&#10007;</span><span><span class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Passport validity:</span> Less than 6 months remaining and/or fewer than 2 blank pages = automatic rejection.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-red-500 font-bold mt-0.5">&#10007;</span><span><span class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Tibet/Xinjiang:</span> Listing these regions on your itinerary triggers extra scrutiny. Apply for a standard itinerary first, then arrange permits separately after visa approval.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-green-600 font-bold mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span><span class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Pro tip:</span> Apply 4-6 weeks before departure. Avoid applying during Chinese national holidays when embassies operate with reduced staff. Keep a photocopy of your passport and visa separate from the originals during your trip.</span></li></ul></div></div></div></section>

<section id="faq" class="section-alt"><div class="container"><div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 reveal"><span class="section-eyebrow">Answers</span><h2 class="heading-lg text-3xl md:text-4xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2></div><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4 stagger-children reveal">
  {faqs.map((f) => (
    <details class="card p-5 cursor-pointer group">
      <summary class="heading-md text-base text-[var(--color-text)] list-none flex items-center justify-between">{f.question}<span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)] transition-transform group-open:rotate-45 text-lg">+</span></summary>
      <p class="body-text text-sm mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-[var(--color-border-light)]" set:html={f.answer}></p>
    </details>
  ))}
</div></div></section><section id="weather" class="section"><div class="container"><div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 reveal"><span class="section-eyebrow">Timing</span><h2 class="heading-lg text-3xl md:text-4xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">When Is the Best Time to Visit China?</h2><p class="body-text text-lg">Month-by-month weather comparison across four key cities. Spring and autumn are ideal.</p><p class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mt-3">Based on long-term climate averages (1991–2020) from the China Meteorological Administration; conditions vary year to year. Temperatures shown as daily low/high.</p></div><div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6 reveal reveal-delay-1"><table class="data-table text-sm"><thead><tr><th>Month</th><th>Beijing</th><th>Shanghai</th><th>Chengdu</th><th>Guilin</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Jan</td><td>−9/2°C · Dry</td><td>1/8°C · Damp</td><td>3/9°C · Overcast</td><td>5/11°C · Cool</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Feb</td><td>−6/5°C · Dry</td><td>2/10°C · Damp</td><td>5/12°C · Cloudy</td><td>7/13°C · Cool</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Mar</td><td>0/12°C · Dusty</td><td>6/15°C · Mild rain</td><td>9/17°C · Mild</td><td>11/17°C · Rainy</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Apr</td><td>8/21°C · Perfect</td><td>11/21°C · Pleasant</td><td>14/23°C · Best</td><td>16/23°C · Humid</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">May</td><td>14/27°C · Warm</td><td>16/26°C · Warm</td><td>19/28°C · Warm</td><td>20/28°C · Rainy</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Jun</td><td>19/31°C · Hot</td><td>21/29°C · Plum rain</td><td>22/30°C · Rainy</td><td>23/31°C · Wet</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Jul</td><td>22/32°C · Humid</td><td>25/33°C · Hot</td><td>24/31°C · Humid</td><td>25/33°C · Hot/wet</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Aug</td><td>21/31°C · Humid</td><td>25/33°C · Typhoon</td><td>23/31°C · Humid</td><td>25/33°C · Hot/wet</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Sep</td><td>15/26°C · Perfect</td><td>21/29°C · Best</td><td>20/27°C · Best</td><td>22/30°C · Good</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Oct</td><td>7/20°C · Best</td><td>15/24°C · Perfect</td><td>15/22°C · Comfort</td><td>17/26°C · Best</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Nov</td><td>0/10°C · Chilly</td><td>9/18°C · Cool</td><td>10/16°C · Cool</td><td>11/20°C · Mild</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Dec</td><td>−6/3°C · Cold</td><td>3/11°C · Cold</td><td>5/11°C · Cool</td><td>7/15°C · Cool</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6 reveal reveal-delay-2"><table class="data-table text-sm"><thead><tr><th>Month</th><th>Best Destination Picks</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Jan</td><td>Beijing, Harbin</td><td>Ice Festival in Harbin; Beijing palaces quiet and half-price hotels</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Feb</td><td>Beijing, Harbin</td><td>Lunar New Year atmosphere; festive, but book transport early</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Mar</td><td>Beijing, Xi&#39;an, Guilin</td><td>Mild spring, fewer crowds; blossom season begins</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Apr</td><td>Beijing, Xi&#39;an, Shanghai</td><td>Prime weather for classic cities; avoid Qingming holiday crowds</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">May</td><td>Guilin, Chengdu, Shanghai</td><td>Warm and green; avoid May 1st Golden Week crowds</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Jun</td><td>Zhangjiajie, Yunnan</td><td>Green mountains at their best; south coast enters rainy season</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Jul</td><td>Yunnan, Zhangjiajie</td><td>Cool highland escapes while Beijing/Shanghai bake; light crowds</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Aug</td><td>Yunnan, Zhangjiajie</td><td>Same cool picks; avoid southern typhoon and peak heat weeks</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Sep</td><td>Beijing, Xi&#39;an, Shanghai</td><td>Autumn begins; clear skies, perfect hiking weather</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Oct</td><td>Guilin, Chengdu, Shanghai</td><td>Arguably the best weather of the year; avoid Oct 1st National Week</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Nov</td><td>Guilin, Guangzhou</td><td>Mild south, fewer tourists, autumn foliage lingers</td></tr><tr><td class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Dec</td><td>Beijing, Harbin</td><td>Minimal crowds and discounted hotels; Harbin Ice Festival opens</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mt-2">Picks cover our 8 guide cities plus Harbin (winter festivals). Peak Chinese holidays (May 1st week, Oct 1st week, Lunar New Year) can push hotel and flight prices 50–100% higher — plan around them.</p></div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 stagger-children reveal"><div class="card p-4 bg-green-50/50 border-green-200"><div class="font-semibold text-sm text-green-800 mb-1">Best Months</div><div class="text-sm text-green-700">April-May, September-October</div><div class="text-xs text-green-600/70 mt-1">Mild temps, clear skies</div></div><div class="card p-4 bg-yellow-50/50 border-yellow-200"><div class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-800 mb-1">Shoulder Season</div><div class="text-sm text-yellow-700">March, June, November</div><div class="text-xs text-yellow-600/70 mt-1">Some weather extremes, fewer crowds</div></div><div class="card p-4 bg-red-50/50 border-red-200"><div class="font-semibold text-sm text-red-800 mb-1">Avoid If Possible</div><div class="text-sm text-red-700">July-August (hot/wet), CNY (chaotic)</div><div class="text-xs text-red-600/70 mt-1">Peak heat, crowds, transport chaos</div></div></div><div class="max-w-3xl mt-12 reveal"><h3 class="heading-md text-2xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">How to Beat the Crowds in 2026</h3><p class="body-text text-sm mb-4">Peak Chinese holidays can push hotel and flight prices 50–100% higher and triple wait times at major sights. Mark these dates and plan around them:</p><div class="card p-5 mb-6"><ul class="space-y-2 body-text text-sm"><li><strong>Qingming Festival (Tomb-Sweeping):</strong> April 4–6, 2026 — classic-city crowds build from April 3.</li><li><strong>Labor Day Golden Week:</strong> May 1–5, 2026 — the busiest domestic travel window of the year.</li><li><strong>National Day Golden Week:</strong> October 1–7, 2026 — trains and flights sell out weeks ahead; avoid entirely if your dates are flexible.</li></ul></div><h4 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">Five Smarter Ways to Sightsee</h4><ol class="space-y-2 body-text text-sm list-decimal list-inside"><li><strong>Pick the right section, not just the attraction.</strong> Great Wall: Jinshanling or Jiankou instead of Badaling. Terracotta Warriors: start at Pit 3 (the quietest) and finish at Pit 1. Forbidden City: walk the side halls first and leave the central axis for later.</li><li><strong>Go early or late.</strong> Hotspots peak between 10am and 3pm. Arrive at 6–8am, or after 4pm when tour groups leave — cooler in summer and better light for photos.</li><li><strong>Swap famous spots for meaningful alternatives.</strong> Xi'an: Lintong Museum (first restored warriors) instead of the main-pit crush. Shanghai: Aurora Museum over the busiest galleries. Beijing: Jingshan Park at sunset instead of a second museum.</li><li><strong>Avoid August 1–15</strong> — the peak of the peak season. If your dates are flexible, late June or early September is noticeably quieter.</li><li><strong>Take trains, not flights, on holiday weekends.</strong> High-speed rail is less affected by holiday booking surges, and stations clear faster than airports.</li></ol><p class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mt-4">Holiday dates above follow 2026 official Chinese public holiday arrangements; always confirm exact dates against official announcements before booking.</p></div></div></section><section class="section-gradient"><div class="container"><div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 reveal"><span class="section-eyebrow">Checklist</span><h2 class="heading-lg text-3xl md:text-4xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">Before Your Trip to China</h2><p class="body-text text-lg">A step-by-step planning timeline from booking flights to setting up payment apps — with practical tips at each stage.</p></div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 stagger-children reveal"><div><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">3-6 Months Before</h3><ul class="space-y-3"><li class="flex items-start gap-3 body-text text-sm"><span class="mt-0.5 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent-light)] text-[var(--color-accent)] flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">1</span>Choose destinations &amp; plan route</li><li class="flex items-start gap-3 body-text text-sm"><span class="mt-0.5 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent-light)] text-[var(--color-accent)] flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">2</span>Book international flights</li><li class="flex items-start gap-3 body-text text-sm"><span class="mt-0.5 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent-light)] text-[var(--color-accent)] flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">3</span>Research visa requirements</li></ul></div><div><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">1-3 Months Before</h3><ul class="space-y-3"><li class="flex items-start gap-3 body-text text-sm"><span class="mt-0.5 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent-light)] text-[var(--color-accent)] flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">4</span>Book hotels &amp; train tickets</li><li class="flex items-start gap-3 body-text text-sm"><span class="mt-0.5 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent-light)] text-[var(--color-accent)] flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">5</span>Apply for visa (if needed)</li><li class="flex items-start gap-3 body-text text-sm"><span class="mt-0.5 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent-light)] text-[var(--color-accent)] flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">6</span>Get travel insurance</li></ul></div><div><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">1-2 Weeks Before</h3><ul class="space-y-3"><li class="flex items-start gap-3 body-text text-sm"><span class="mt-0.5 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent-light)] text-[var(--color-accent)] flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">7</span>Set up Alipay / WeChat Pay</li><li class="flex items-start gap-3 body-text text-sm"><span class="mt-0.5 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent-light)] text-[var(--color-accent)] flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">8</span>Get an eSIM or VPN</li><li class="flex items-start gap-3 body-text text-sm"><span class="mt-0.5 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent-light)] text-[var(--color-accent)] flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">9</span>Download China travel apps</li></ul></div><div><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">Before Departure</h3><ul class="space-y-3"><li class="flex items-start gap-3 body-text text-sm"><span class="mt-0.5 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent-light)] text-[var(--color-accent)] flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">10</span>Save hotel addresses in Chinese</li><li class="flex items-start gap-3 body-text text-sm"><span class="mt-0.5 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent-light)] text-[var(--color-accent)] flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">11</span>Prepare passport &amp; backup docs</li><li class="flex items-start gap-3 body-text text-sm"><span class="mt-0.5 w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent-light)] text-[var(--color-accent)] flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">12</span>Payment backup (cash + card)</li></ul></div></div></div></section><section id="clothing" class="section"><div class="container"><div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 reveal"><span class="section-eyebrow">What to Wear</span><h2 class="heading-lg text-3xl md:text-4xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">What to Pack & Wear by Season</h2><p class="body-text text-lg">China spans five climate zones. What you pack depends entirely on when and where you go. Here is your season-by-season clothing guide.</p></div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4 stagger-children reveal"><div class="card p-5"><h3 class="heading-md text-base text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Spring (Mar-May)</h3><div class="tag mb-2">8-25C</div><p class="body-text text-xs mb-3"><strong>Wear:</strong> Light jacket, long-sleeve shirts, comfortable pants. Northern cities still chilly in March.</p><p class="body-text text-xs mb-2"><strong>Bring:</strong> Lightweight rain jacket, scarf for Beijing mornings</p><p class="body-text text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] italic">Layer up - mornings can be 8C while afternoons hit 22C in Beijing.</p></div><div class="card p-5"><h3 class="heading-md text-base text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Summer (Jun-Aug)</h3><div class="tag mb-2">22-35C</div><p class="body-text text-xs mb-3"><strong>Wear:</strong> Breathable fabrics: cotton, linen, moisture-wicking. Shorts and t-shirts fine.</p><p class="body-text text-xs mb-2"><strong>Bring:</strong> Sunscreen SPF50+, wide-brim hat, sunglasses, insect repellent (Guilin/Yunnan)</p><p class="body-text text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] italic">Carry an umbrella for sudden thunderstorms. Temples require covered shoulders and knees.</p></div><div class="card p-5"><h3 class="heading-md text-base text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Autumn (Sep-Nov)</h3><div class="tag mb-2">10-25C</div><p class="body-text text-xs mb-3"><strong>Wear:</strong> Sweater or fleece, light jacket, long pants. Northern cities need a warm coat by November.</p><p class="body-text text-xs mb-2"><strong>Bring:</strong> Comfortable hiking shoes for Great Wall/karst trails, light gloves for October</p><p class="body-text text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] italic">The golden season - dress for outdoor exploration. October is crisp and perfect.</p></div><div class="card p-5"><h3 class="heading-md text-base text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Winter (Dec-Feb)</h3><div class="tag mb-2">-10-12C</div><p class="body-text text-xs mb-3"><strong>Wear:</strong> Thermal base layer, thick sweater, down jacket, warm socks, insulated boots.</p><p class="body-text text-xs mb-2"><strong>Bring:</strong> Gloves, beanie, scarf, lip balm, moisturizer (central heating is very dry)</p><p class="body-text text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] italic">Beijing can hit -10C; Shanghai stays at 1-8C damp cold; Guangzhou is mild at 10-18C.</p></div></div></div></section><section id="packing" class="section-alt"><div class="container"><div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 reveal"><span class="section-eyebrow">Packing List</span><h2 class="heading-lg text-3xl md:text-4xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">Complete China Packing Checklist</h2><p class="body-text text-lg">Print this or save it offline. These items make the difference between a smooth trip and a stressful one.</p></div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5 stagger-children reveal"><div class="card p-5"><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">Documents</h3><ul class="space-y-2"><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Passport (6+ months validity)</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Printed visa or eVisa confirmation</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Travel insurance documents</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Hotel booking confirmations (in Chinese)</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Printed flight itinerary for visa-on-arrival</span></li></ul></div><div class="card p-5"><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">Tech &amp; Money</h3><ul class="space-y-2"><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Unlocked smartphone (install VPN first)</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">eSIM or local SIM card</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Power bank (20,000mAh max)</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Universal power adapter (Type A/C/I)</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Activated Alipay + linked foreign card</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">$200-500 emergency cash</span></li></ul></div><div class="card p-5"><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">Health &amp; Comfort</h3><ul class="space-y-2"><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Prescription meds (original packaging)</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">N95/KN95 masks (Nov-Mar pollution)</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Hand sanitizer &amp; wet wipes</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Mosquito repellent (Guilin, Yunnan)</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Travel-sized toilet paper (public toilets often lack it)</span></li></ul></div><div class="card p-5"><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">Clothing</h3><ul class="space-y-2"><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Most comfortable walking shoes (15,000+ steps daily)</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Light scarf/wrap (temple cover-up + warmth)</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Quick-dry underwear &amp; socks</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Rain jacket or compact umbrella</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-2 text-sm"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-0.5">&#10003;</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">One nice outfit for fine dining/upscale hotels</span></li></ul></div></div></div></section><section class="section-alt"><div class="container"><div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 reveal"><span class="section-eyebrow">Getting Around</span><h2 class="heading-lg text-3xl md:text-4xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">How to Travel Around China</h2><p class="body-text text-lg">China transport is world-class. Here is what to use and when.</p></div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5 stagger-children reveal"><div class="card p-6"><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">High-Speed Rail (高铁)</h3><p class="body-text text-sm mb-1 text-[var(--color-accent)] font-medium">Intercity travel under 1,000km</p><p class="body-text text-sm">Book on Trip.com or 12306.cn (Chinese only). G-trains fastest (300 km/h). Second class ~¥0.45/km. Book 2+ weeks ahead for holidays. Stations require passport + security check.</p></div><div class="card p-6"><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">Domestic Flights</h3><p class="body-text text-sm mb-1 text-[var(--color-accent)] font-medium">Crossing the country (1,500+ km)</p><p class="body-text text-sm">Book on Trip.com. Major airlines: Air China, China Southern, China Eastern. Budget: Spring Airlines. Arrive 2h early. Delays common — build buffer.</p></div><div class="card p-6"><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">Metro / Subway</h3><p class="body-text text-sm mb-1 text-[var(--color-accent)] font-medium">City navigation</p><p class="body-text text-sm">Every major city has one. ¥3–9 per ride. English signs/stops announced. Buy ticket at machines (English mode). Alipay transport QR works in most cities.</p></div><div class="card p-6"><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">Didi (Ride-Hailing)</h3><p class="body-text text-sm mb-1 text-[var(--color-accent)] font-medium">Door-to-door, luggage, late night</p><p class="body-text text-sm">China&#39;s Uber. Download DiDi Great China (English interface). Link foreign card. Cheaper than taxis. Auto-translate messaging with driver.</p></div><div class="card p-6"><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">Public Bus</h3><p class="body-text text-sm mb-1 text-[var(--color-accent)] font-medium">Budget city travel</p><p class="body-text text-sm">¥1–3 per ride. Scan Alipay transport code. Routes in Chinese — use map app. Bus #5 in Beijing passes major sites.</p></div><div class="card p-6"><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-2">Bike Share (共享单车)</h3><p class="body-text text-sm mb-1 text-[var(--color-accent)] font-medium">Short hops, neighborhoods</p><p class="body-text text-sm">Meituan/Hellobike everywhere. Scan QR via Alipay mini-program. ¥1.5 per 30 min. Dedicated bike lanes in most cities.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 reveal"><span class="section-eyebrow">Essentials</span><h2 class="heading-lg text-3xl md:text-4xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">Payment &amp; Internet in China</h2><p class="body-text text-lg">Two things every traveler worries about. Here is exactly how to set up payments and stay connected.</p></div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8"><div><h3 class="heading-md text-xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">Setting Up Alipay (Step by Step)</h3><div class="space-y-4"><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-1"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">1</span><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Download before departure</span></div><p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] ml-9">Get Alipay from App Store / Google Play. Register with international phone number.</p></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-1"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">2</span><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Verify identity</span></div><p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] ml-9">Me → Settings → Account &amp; Security → Identity Verification. Upload passport photo. Takes 1–24 hours.</p></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-1"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">3</span><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Add card</span></div><p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] ml-9">Me → Bank Cards → Add Card. Visa, Mastercard, Amex all supported. Small verification charge refunded.</p></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-1"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">4</span><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Test before arriving</span></div><p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] ml-9">Try a small purchase on Trip.com or Didi. Tour Pass is alternative if card linking fails.</p></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-1"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">5</span><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Pay in China</span></div><p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] ml-9">Two ways: (1) Scan merchant QR → enter amount → pay. (2) Show your QR → merchant scans it. Both work.</p></div></div></div><div><h3 class="heading-md text-xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">Other Essentials</h3><div class="space-y-4"><div class="card p-4"><h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">eSIM &amp; Internet</h4><p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Get an eSIM before departure (Airalo, Holafly) or buy a local SIM at the airport. Install a reliable VPN before arriving.</p></div><div class="card p-4"><h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">WeChat Pay</h4><p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Alternative to Alipay, also supports foreign cards. Stricter verification than Alipay. Some smaller vendors only accept WeChat Pay.</p></div><div class="card p-4"><h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Credit Cards</h4><p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Accepted at major hotels and upscale restaurants. Mobile payment is essential for daily purchases. Carry cash as backup.</p></div><div class="card p-4"><h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Essential Apps</h4><p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Trip.com (booking), Didi (rides), Alipay (payments), Pleco (dictionary), Metroman (metro maps).</p></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)] bg-amber-50/30"><div class="container max-w-3xl py-8"><h3 class="heading-md text-lg text-[var(--color-text)] mb-3">Setting Up WeChat Pay (Backup Option)</h3><div class="space-y-3"><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-1"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">1</span><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Download WeChat</span></div><p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] ml-9">Available on all app stores. Register with your phone number. You may need an existing WeChat user to scan a QR code for account verification.</p></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-1"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">2</span><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Enable WeChat Pay</span></div><p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] ml-9">Me → Services → Wallet → Add Bank Card. Verify with passport photo. WeChat Pay verification is stricter for foreigners — start with Alipay first as it is more foreigner-friendly.</p></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-1"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-[var(--color-accent)] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">3</span><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Pro Tip</span></div><p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] ml-9">Even if you cannot link a card, WeChat is still essential for communication — most hotels, tour guides, and locals use it. Download it regardless. Mini-programs within WeChat are also the gateway to booking train tickets, museum tickets, and more.</p></div></div><p class="body-text text-xs mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">Having both Alipay and WeChat Pay set up gives you a backup if one fails. Alipay is friendlier for foreign credit cards, while WeChat is more widely used for messaging and mini-programs (ticket booking, food ordering, bike sharing).</p></div></section><section class="section-alt"><div class="container"><div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 reveal"><span class="section-eyebrow">Language</span><h2 class="heading-lg text-3xl md:text-4xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">Essential Chinese for Travelers</h2><p class="body-text text-lg">Fifteen phrases that will make your trip smoother. Save this page for offline access.</p></div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4 stagger-children reveal"><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-1"><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Hello</span><span class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] font-mono">Nǐ hǎo</span></div><div class="text-lg text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-1 flex items-center gap-1"><span>你好</span> <button class="speak-btn text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity" data-text="你好" title="Listen to pronunciation">&#9654;</button></div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Universal greeting, any time of day</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-1"><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Thank you</span><span class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] font-mono">Xiè xie</span></div><div class="text-lg text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-1 flex items-center gap-1"><span>谢谢</span> <button class="speak-btn text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity" data-text="谢谢" title="Listen to pronunciation">&#9654;</button></div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Use generously — appreciated everywhere</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-1"><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">How much?</span><span class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] font-mono">Duō shǎo qián?</span></div><div class="text-lg text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-1 flex items-center gap-1"><span>多少钱？</span> <button class="speak-btn text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity" data-text="多少钱？" title="Listen to pronunciation">&#9654;</button></div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Shopping in markets. Point at item while asking</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-1"><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Too expensive!</span><span class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] font-mono">Tài guì le!</span></div><div class="text-lg text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-1 flex items-center gap-1"><span>太贵了！</span> <button class="speak-btn text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity" data-text="太贵了！" title="Listen to pronunciation">&#9654;</button></div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Essential for market bargaining. Say it with a smile</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-1"><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">I don&#39;t understand</span><span class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] font-mono">Wǒ tīng bù dǒng</span></div><div class="text-lg text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-1 flex items-center gap-1"><span>我听不懂</span> <button class="speak-btn text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity" data-text="我听不懂" title="Listen to pronunciation">&#9654;</button></div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">When someone speaks fast. Follow with translation app</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-1"><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Where is the toilet?</span><span class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] font-mono">Xǐshǒujiān zài nǎlǐ?</span></div><div class="text-lg text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-1 flex items-center gap-1"><span>洗手间在哪里？</span> <button class="speak-btn text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity" data-text="洗手间在哪里？" title="Listen to pronunciation">&#9654;</button></div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Most restaurants and malls have clean public toilets</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-1"><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">No spicy</span><span class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] font-mono">Bú yào là</span></div><div class="text-lg text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-1 flex items-center gap-1"><span>不要辣</span> <button class="speak-btn text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity" data-text="不要辣" title="Listen to pronunciation">&#9654;</button></div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Crucial in Sichuan. Show this on your phone if needed</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-1"><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">The bill, please</span><span class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] font-mono">Mǎi dān</span></div><div class="text-lg text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-1 flex items-center gap-1"><span>买单</span> <button class="speak-btn text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity" data-text="买单" title="Listen to pronunciation">&#9654;</button></div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">At restaurants. Also works as hand gesture (writing in air)</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-1"><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">This one</span><span class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] font-mono">Zhè ge</span></div><div class="text-lg text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-1 flex items-center gap-1"><span>这个</span> <button class="speak-btn text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity" data-text="这个" title="Listen to pronunciation">&#9654;</button></div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Menu ordering: point at picture + say this</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-1"><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Delicious!</span><span class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] font-mono">Hǎo chī!</span></div><div class="text-lg text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-1 flex items-center gap-1"><span>好吃！</span> <button class="speak-btn text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity" data-text="好吃！" title="Listen to pronunciation">&#9654;</button></div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Best compliment you can give. Chefs will beam</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-1"><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">I&#39;m vegetarian</span><span class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] font-mono">Wǒ chī sù</span></div><div class="text-lg text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-1 flex items-center gap-1"><span>我吃素</span> <button class="speak-btn text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity" data-text="我吃素" title="Listen to pronunciation">&#9654;</button></div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Important: many dishes hide meat broth. Be explicit</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="flex items-baseline justify-between mb-1"><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)]">Take me here</span><span class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] font-mono">Qǐng dài wǒ qù zhèlǐ</span></div><div class="text-lg text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-1 flex items-center gap-1"><span>请带我去这里</span> <button class="speak-btn text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] hover:text-[var(--col