[var(--color-text-muted)] hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] opacity-40 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity" data-text="我需要帮助" title="Listen to pronunciation">&#9654;</button></div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">For emergencies. Chinese people are very helpful to tourists</div></div></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 reveal"><span class="section-eyebrow">Cuisine</span><h2 class="heading-lg text-3xl md:text-4xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">What to Eat in China: City by City</h2><p class="body-text text-lg">Each city has its own food identity. Here is what to eat and where to find it.</p></div><div class="food-tabs" id="food-tabs"><div class="food-tab-nav mb-6 overflow-x-auto"><button data-tab="0" class="food-tab-btn">Beijing</button><button data-tab="1" class="food-tab-btn">Shanghai</button><button data-tab="2" class="food-tab-btn">Chengdu</button><button data-tab="3" class="food-tab-btn">Xi&#39;an</button><button data-tab="4" class="food-tab-btn">Guangzhou</button><button data-tab="5" class="food-tab-btn">Guilin</button></div><div data-tab="0" class="food-tab-panel"><div class="max-w-3xl"><h3 class="heading-md text-xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Beijing <span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">北京</span></h3><p class="body-text text-sm mb-6 text-[var(--color-accent)] font-medium">Peking Duck &amp; Imperial cuisine</p><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4"><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Peking Duck</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Siji Minfu (四季民福)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Crispy skin, tender meat, wrapped with hoisin, cucumber, spring onion</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Zhajiang Noodles</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Old Beijing Noodle King (老北京炸酱面大王)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Thick wheat noodles with fermented soybean paste, cucumber, pork</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Mongolian Hot Pot</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Donglaishun (东来顺)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Copper pot with charcoal, thin-sliced mutton, sesame dip</div></div></div></div></div><div data-tab="1" class="food-tab-panel"><div class="max-w-3xl"><h3 class="heading-md text-xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Shanghai <span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">上海</span></h3><p class="body-text text-sm mb-6 text-[var(--color-accent)] font-medium">Soup dumplings &amp; sweet-savory</p><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4"><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Xiaolongbao</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Jia Jia Tang Bao (佳家汤包)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Steamed soup dumplings filled with pork and hot broth</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Shengjianbao</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Da Hu Chun (大壶春)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Pan-fried pork buns with crispy bottom and juicy filling</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Hairy Crab (Sep–Nov)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Cheng Long Hang (成隆行)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Seasonal steamed mitten crab with ginger vinegar</div></div></div></div></div><div data-tab="2" class="food-tab-panel"><div class="max-w-3xl"><h3 class="heading-md text-xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Chengdu <span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">成都</span></h3><p class="body-text text-sm mb-6 text-[var(--color-accent)] font-medium">Sichuan — numbingly spicy</p><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4"><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Sichuan Hot Pot</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Shujiuxiang (蜀九香)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Fiery broth with Sichuan peppercorns, meats, tofu, vegetables</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Mapo Tofu</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Chen Mapo Tofu (陈麻婆豆腐)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Silken tofu in chili-bean paste with minced pork, numbing</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Dan Dan Noodles</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Street stalls (路边摊)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Noodles with chili oil, sesame paste, minced pork, scallions</div></div></div></div></div><div data-tab="3" class="food-tab-panel"><div class="max-w-3xl"><h3 class="heading-md text-xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Xi&#39;an <span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">西安</span></h3><p class="body-text text-sm mb-6 text-[var(--color-accent)] font-medium">Noodles &amp; Muslim street food</p><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4"><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Biangbiang Noodles</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Muslim Quarter (回民街)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Belt-wide hand-pulled noodles with chili oil, garlic</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Lamb Paomo</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Tongshengxiang (同盛祥)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Crumbled flatbread in rich lamb broth with vermicelli</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Roujiamo</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Fan Ji (樊记)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Braised pork belly in crispy flatbread — original Chinese burger</div></div></div></div></div><div data-tab="4" class="food-tab-panel"><div class="max-w-3xl"><h3 class="heading-md text-xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Guangzhou <span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">广州</span></h3><p class="body-text text-sm mb-6 text-[var(--color-accent)] font-medium">Dim sum capital of the world</p><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4"><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Har Gow (Shrimp Dumpling)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Panxi (泮溪酒家)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Translucent wrapper, whole shrimp filling, delicate</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Siu Mai</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Panxi (泮溪酒家)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Open-top pork and shrimp dumpling, yellow wrapper</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">White Cut Chicken</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Wenji (文记壹心鸡)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Poached chicken at perfect temperature, ginger-scallion oil</div></div></div></div></div><div data-tab="5" class="food-tab-panel"><div class="max-w-3xl"><h3 class="heading-md text-xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Guilin <span class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">桂林</span></h3><p class="body-text text-sm mb-6 text-[var(--color-accent)] font-medium">Rice noodles &amp; river fish</p><div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4"><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Guilin Mifen</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">Chongshan (崇善米粉)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Rice noodles in bone broth with pickled beans, peanuts, chili</div></div><div class="card p-4"><div class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] mb-1">Beer Fish</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-accent)] mb-2">West Street riverside (西街江边)</div><div class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Yangshuo river fish braised in local beer with tomatoes</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 reveal"><span class="section-eyebrow">About This Guide</span><h2 class="heading-lg text-3xl md:text-4xl text-[var(--color-text)] mb-4">Why You Can Trust China Trips</h2><p class="body-text text-lg">Independent, researched, and kept current. No AI-generated filler. No sponsored rankings.</p></div><div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-8 stagger-children reveal"><div class="card p-5 text-center"><div class="key-number text-2xl">8</div><p class="body-text text-xs mt-2">Major Chinese cities researched in depth</p></div><div class="card p-5 text-center"><div class="key-number text-2xl">54</div><p class="body-text text-xs mt-2">Countries of visa information verified</p></div><div class="card p-5 text-center"><div class="key-number text-2xl">12</div><p class="body-text text-xs mt-2">Months of weather data per city</p></div><div class="card p-5 text-center"><div class="key-number text-2xl">100+</div><p class="body-text text-xs mt-2">Restaurants, hotels, and attractions reviewed</p></div></div><div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto card p-6 reveal reveal-delay-2"><p class="body-text text-sm">China Trips is an independent travel guide created and maintained by travelers who have collectively spent years exploring China — from navigating Chengdu alleyways to cycling Yangshuo rice paddies, from bargaining in Beijing markets to hiking Tiger Leaping Gorge. Every itinerary, budget estimate, restaurant recommendation, and practical tip is based on firsthand experience. Our destination coverage includes multiple <a href="https://whc.unesco.org/en/statesparties/cn" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">UNESCO World Heritage sites</a> across China. Prices and policies are verified regularly (last full verification: <strong>August 2026</strong>). We do not accept payment for listings or rankings. <a href="/about" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Learn more about our team</a> and research process. If something is wrong, <a href="mailto:hello@chinatripzone.com" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">tell us</a> and we will fix it.</p></div></div></section><section class="relative overflow-hidden"><div class="absolute inset-0"><img src="/images/hero/hero.webp" alt="China landscape" class="h-full w-full object-cover" loading="lazy" width="1920" height="1249"><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-stone-900/75"></div></div><div class="relative z-10 max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-24 md:py-32 text-center"><p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.2em] text-[var(--color-accent)] uppercase mb-5">Ready to Go</p><h2 class="heading-lg text-3xl md:text-5xl text-white leading-tight mb-5">Your China Trip Starts Here</h2><p class="text-white/70 text-lg max-w-xl mx-auto leading-relaxed mb-8">All the research in one place. Itineraries, budgets, visas, packing lists, and honest city guides — all from firsthand travel experience. Free. Independent. Updated. <a href="/about" class="text-white/70 hover:text-white underline">About us</a></p><div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3"><a href="#planner" class="btn-primary">Plan My Trip</a><a href="#destinations" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center font-medium text-sm px-7 py-3 rounded-lg border border-white/40 text-white bg-white/10 backdrop-blur-sm 